#Title under load
#Composer SuperForge (procedural)
#Tempo 54

; smelter's own song, and the FOURTH in the tree. The other three are spoken
; for and none of them is this: `slice_b_song` is the room rail's ambient piece
; (its composed rest half-bar is the window a reverb A/B is measured in),
; `drive_song` is the action rails' D minor shooter piece, and `circuit_song`
; is A mixolydian for a lap. This one is a MACHINE HALL under load -- four
; steel plates rising and falling on four different harmonics over a cavern of
; molten metal, none of them ever in step (game/smelter/game.toml describes the
; picture). The music is written to be that, not to accompany it: what a
; listener should hear is a machine CYCLE, not a tune.
;
; =============================================================================
; THE THREE PERIODS, AND WHY THEY ARE COPRIME-ISH
; =============================================================================
; This is the piece's whole rhythmic idea and it is stated here rather than
; left to be counted off the ticks. Three parts run at three different lengths:
;
;     the ostinato  (!mc, channel B)   42 ticks   = 7 sixteenths
;     the strikes   (!an, channel E)   32 ticks   = 1 1/3 beats
;     the press     (!kk, channel F)   96 ticks   = one 4/4 bar
;
; 42 = 2*3*7 and 32 = 2^5 and 96 = 2^5*3, so the least common multiple is
; 2^5*3*7 = 672 ticks -- SEVEN bars. Inside those seven bars no two of the
; three ever repeat their alignment: the ostinato's head walks 18 ticks (three
; quarters of a beat) further into the bar on every repeat, and the strikes
; land on the downbeat and then never on another beat until the cycle closes.
; That drift IS the plates never being in step, and it is the reason none of
; the three is allowed to be a bar long except the press.
;
; The song loops at 1344 ticks -- TWO of those 672-tick cycles, fourteen bars,
; about 31 seconds. So the ostinato repeats 32 times and the strikes 42, which
; is the two periods swapped and is just 32*42 = 1344 read from the other end.
;
; WHY THE HALVES DIFFER. Cycle 1 carries the ratchet (channel D); cycle 2
; carries the lead (channel A) and the ratchet stops. With every part sounding
; for all fourteen bars the loop has no shape at all, and repetition that never
; changes register stops reading as relentless and starts reading as stuck.
; drive_song makes the same split for the same reason.
;
; =============================================================================
; THE HARMONY
; =============================================================================
; C minor, and darker than anything else in the tree. The key signature is the
; three flats of C natural minor (`-bea`, so `e` `a` `b` are already E flat,
; A flat, B flat) and NOT the four of C Phrygian -- which is the point: the
; FLAT SECOND has to be written `d-` every single time it appears, so every
; occurrence is a deliberate accidental on the page instead of a scale degree
; that arrived for free. The tritone is `g-` and is spelled the same way.
;
; Those two notes are the machine's fault, and they are used at two different
; densities on purpose:
;
;   * MACHINED IN. The ostinato contains both -- C, D flat, C, G, G flat, F --
;     so the rub and the tritone recur every 42 ticks. An ostinato that
;     varied would not be one, and a fault a machine has is a fault it has on
;     every stroke.
;   * SPARING. The bass pedal is a C for six bars and then grinds to D flat
;     for half of the seventh (a minor NINTH under the ostinato's root) before
;     resetting. Once every 672 ticks, which is the only place in the piece
;     the floor itself moves.
;
; The lead over cycle 2 is a slow descent -- C E- F | G G- | F E- D- | C |
; A- G | F G- F | E- D- C -- whose two turns are exactly those two intervals:
; the G falling to G flat, and the F leaning on G flat and back.
;
; =============================================================================
; ECHO, AND THE TWO NUMBERS THAT ARE NOT THIS SONG'S TO PICK
; =============================================================================
; 96 ms of buffer (12 KiB of ARAM) behind a heavily low-passed FIR: a long,
; dark tail with almost no top in it, which is a concrete hall with steel in
; it rather than drive_song's 64 ms slap or the room's 128 ms cavern. Taps sum
; to 127; the compiler rejects an absolute sum over 128.
;
; #EchoVolume 12 and #EchoFeedback 24 ARE NOT A CHOICE. They are a tree-wide
; constant that lives in the sound-effect definitions rather than in any song:
; `room_a_ambience` and `beam_end` write those two values back as LITERALS as
; the dry rest state, so a song whose header disagrees leaves any rail using
; those effects in a rest state it was never in, permanently, after the first
; use. drive_song was authored at 10/20 and a red landing gate is how that was
; found. Buffer length and FIR stay per-song because nothing writes them back.
#EchoLength 96
#EchoVolume 12
#EchoFeedback 24
#FirFilter 56 40 24 6 1 0 0 0

#KeySignature -bea

@1 square_lead
@2 saw
@3 tri_bass
@4 pluck
@5 step
@6 kick

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE PERCUSSION IS SAMPLES AND NEVER `N`. There is exactly one noise
; generator, and the driver zeroes the volume of every music channel sharing
; it the moment a sound effect wants it (audio-driver.asm, the `SfxNoise`
; branch). This rail's cues are `select` and `chime`, neither of which takes
; noise -- but `explosion`, `hit` and `skid` are in the same shared blob and
; any rail could grow one, so a noise part here would be a part that vanishes
; the day it does. `kick` and `step` are the two drum samples the tree has and
; they are what this kit is made of.
;
; `bell` is deliberately NOT used anywhere in this song. It is what `chime`
; is voiced by, and `chime` is this rail's departure cue -- keeping the bell
; out of the music is what makes a bell in the mix mean "the player pressed
; Start" to a listener as well as to a test reading VxSRCN.
;
; K0 disables key-off on both drum channels: these are one-shots that decay to
; zero on their own and a key-off would choke the kick's tail. Their gaps are
; therefore `w` waits and never `r` rests -- a rest still keys off under K0.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

; --- !mc: THE MACHINE CYCLE. 42 ticks. -------------------------------------
; An eighth-note stamp on the root, then five sixteenths: the flat second
; leaning on the root and falling back, then the fifth walking down
; chromatically G - G flat - F into the next stamp. Six events, seven
; sixteenths of length, and it is the only melodic material in the first half
; of the loop.
!mc o3 c%12 d-%6 c%6 g%6 g-%6 f%6

; --- !rs: the ratchet. 32 ticks. -------------------------------------------
; Three short plucks a long way up -- C, D flat, C -- the same semitone rub
; the ostinato has, at the top of the mix and on the strikes' period rather
; than the ostinato's. It runs in cycle 1 only.
!rs o4 c%3 r%5 d-%3 r%5 c%3 r%13

; --- !an: metal on metal. 32 ticks. ----------------------------------------
; A bright ping hard right and a deep clank hard left, 12 ticks apart, three
; times a bar. Against a 24-tick beat that puts hits at ticks 0, 12, 32, 44,
; 64 and 76 of every bar: ONE of the six is on a beat and the other five are
; not, which is what "syncopated, not a backbeat" means here. The pan
; alternation is why this rail sets TadAudioMode::STEREO.
!an v12 o5 p92 c%6 w%6 v15 o3 p36 c%6 w%14

; --- !kk: the press. 96 ticks. ---------------------------------------------
; Six-four-six sixteenths: a limping three-stroke bar that is deliberately not
; 2+2+2+2. It is the only part whose period IS the bar, so it is the grid the
; other two are heard to drift against.
!kk o2 c%36 c%24 c%36

; ---- A: the lead, cycle 2 only. Wide vibrato, wet, and the only part of the
;         piece that is a line rather than a loop. Sustaining ADSR because a
;         warning horn does not decay; Q7 to keep the note ends articulated.
; EVERY BAR CARRIES ITS OWN OCTAVE so a stray `>` cannot leak into the next --
; the class of mistake that is invisible in MML and obvious on the chip.
; Nothing is written to G or H on any channel: those are the two the driver
; ducks while a sound effect plays, so a part written there would vanish every
; time this rail's B or Start cue fired.
A  L @1 v11 E1 Q7 A13,2,7,5 MP18,l16,l16
A  r1 r1 r1 r1 r1 r1 r1
A  o4 c2 e4 f4                | o4 g2. g-4              | o4 f2 e4 d-4
A  o4 c1                      | o4 a2 g2                | o4 f2 g-4 f4
A  o4 e2 d-4 c4

; ---- B: the ostinato. Saw, dry, slightly left, and it never stops. 32 turns
;         of a 42-tick figure is the whole loop.
B  L @2 v14 E0 Q6 A15,3,3,14 p56
B  [!mc ]32

; ---- C: the pedal -- the plant hum. Triangle two octaves under the melody,
;         dry (a wet drone smears everything above it), on an ADSR that
;         sustains flat so a whole-note re-strike reads as a motor breathing
;         rather than as a note dying. Six bars of C, then the D flat grind
;         and the reset. Twice.
C  L @3 v13 E0 A6,2,7,0 o2
C  [c1]6 d-2 c2
C  [c1]6 d-2 c2

; ---- D: the ratchet, cycle 1 only. Quiet, wet, hard right.
D  L @4 v8 E1 p100
D  [!rs ]21
D  r1 r1 r1 r1 r1 r1 r1

; ---- E: the strikes.     ---- F: the press.
; Both under K0, both samples, neither anywhere near the noise generator.
E  L @5 K0 E1
E  [!an ]42
F  L @6 v16 K0 E0 p64
F  [!kk ]14
